  "solution": "BODMAS Table: \n\n [IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/d50192f098c21078501d30eeafe1a8c64bc30dd9621c48caa8a39ffc60f68b64.png] \n\nGiven equation: 18 + 3 − 6 × 2 ÷ 5 = ?\n\n \n \n\n **+**\n **-**\n **×**\n **÷**\n \n \n\n **×**\n **+**\n **÷**\n **-**\n \n \n\nNow, replacing the symbols:\n\n⇒ 18 × 3 + 6 ÷ 2 - 5 = ?\n\n⇒ __**18 × 3**__ + 6 ÷ 2 - 5 = ?\n\n⇒ 54 + __**6 ÷ 2**__ - 5 = ?\n\n⇒ 54 + __**3 - 5**__ = ?\n\n⇒ 54 + __**-2**__ = ?\n\n⇒ __**52**__.\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"Option 4\".",
